   "evidence": "`Scalar.lean:213-217` defines the generic `instSMulOfNormedAlgebra` and `coe_smul_of_normedAlgebra` for any `\ud835\udd5c'`. `Support.lean:125` `tsupport_smul` covers only the base field `\ud835\udd5c`. `Basic.lean:493-500` reproves the same law with `simp only [..., coe_smul_of_normedAlgebra, Pi.smul_apply]; exact not_congr (smul_eq_zero_iff_right hz)`, which uses nothing specific to \u2102 or to complexification.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/VectorBundle/Section/CompactSupport/Complexification/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "In `Section/Support.lean`, add `tsupport_smul_of_normedAlgebra (c : \ud835\udd5c') (s : C\u209b^n\u27eeI; F, W\u27ef) (hc : c \u2260 0) : (c \u2022 s).tsupport = s.tsupport`, assuming `[\u2200 x, Module \ud835\udd5c' (W x)]` with fibres satisfying `NoZeroSMulDivisors \ud835\udd5c' (W x)`. Then derive `tsupport_I_smul` from it and delete `tsupport_complex_smul`.",
   "issue": "`tsupport_complex_smul` proves that a nonzero scalar preserves support only for `z : \u2102` on `C\u209b^n\u27eeI; Complexification F, fun x \u21a6 \u2102 \u2297[\u211d] V x\u27ef`. The proof only uses `coe_smul_of_normedAlgebra` and `smul_eq_zero_iff_right`, so it holds for any normed-algebra scalar `c : \ud835\udd5c'` acting on sections through `instSMulOfNormedAlgebra`. Stating it inside the complexification compact-support leaf repeats, as a special case, the argument of the existing `tsupport_smul`.",
